# Alembic Migrations

Database migrations for the Task Management API (SQLAlchemy + Alembic, SQLite).

## Usage

Run all commands from the **project root** (where `alembic.ini` lives), with the virtual environment activated:

```bash
alembic upgrade head                              # Apply all pending migrations
alembic current                                   # Show current revision
alembic history                                   # List migration history
alembic downgrade -1                              # Roll back one revision
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description"  # Generate a migration from model changes
alembic revision -m "description"                 # Create an empty migration template
```

## Migrations

| Revision | Description |
|---|---|
| `44840f774604` | Initial `tasks` table |

> **Note:** Never use `Base.metadata.create_all()` to create tables — always use Alembic so schema changes are tracked and reproducible.
